[111.218, "o", "\u001b[1;35m\u23fa Claude\u001b[0m\r\n  Done. Summary:\r\n  \r\n  - **`src/data/universities.json`** \u2014 84 real universities: 22 North America, 24 Europe, 20 Asia, 8 Oceania, 10 Middl\r\n  e East, matching the CLAUDE.md data model exactly (id, name, country, city, region, minGPA, acceptanceRate, fields, \r\n  tuitionIntlUSD, livingCostUSD, applicationFeeUSD, ranking, website). Selectivity is split roughly into quarters (21 \r\n  elite / 23 strong / 20 solid / 20 accessible), each with 3\u20136 canonical field tags and realistic tuition/living/fee/r\r\n  anking estimates (e.g. German/Swiss publics near-zero tuition, US private elites ~$58\u201365k, UK/Asia/Oceania priced pe\r\n  r real patterns).\r\n  - **`src/lib/loadUniversities.js`** \u2014 imports the JSON and adds the derived `totalAnnualUSD` field.\r\n  - **`scripts/validate-data.mjs`** \u2014 checks required keys, region/tag validity, numeric ranges, id uniqueness, and we\r\n  bsite format; added as `npm run validate`.\r\n  \r\n  `npm run validate` passes (84/84 OK) and `npm run build` still succeeds.\r\n\r\n"]
